@*
    Verification Guidance Component
    Shows how to verify independently through channels the user already has,
    so they never rely on contact details supplied by a possible scammer.
    Status: DRAFT content from CONTENT-LIBRARY.md
*@

<section class="verification-guidance" aria-labelledby="verify-title">
    <div class="verification-head">
        <h2 id="verify-title"><i class="bi bi-patch-check" aria-hidden="true"></i> To verify independently</h2>
        <span class="badge badge-draft">Draft</span>
    </div>

    <div class="row g-3">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="guidance-box guidance-do">
                <h3><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill" aria-hidden="true"></i> Do use</h3>
                <ul class="guidance-list">
                    <li>The number on your physical card or old bills, not a number they just gave you</li>
                    <li>Official contacts you found yourself (type the website yourself, don’t click their link)</li>
                    <li>A number you saved before this happened</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="guidance-box guidance-dont">
                <h3><i class="bi bi-x-circle-fill" aria-hidden="true"></i> Never use</h3>
                <ul class="guidance-list guidance-list-negative">
                    <li>A phone number they just told you</li>
                    <li>A link or website they sent you</li>
                    <li>An app they asked you to download</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <p class="verification-why">
        <strong>Why this matters:</strong> scammers often give you fake “verification” numbers that they control.
        Real verification means using a contact you found independently.
    </p>
</section>
